  "methodology": "SmolLM2-1.7B, CUDA bf16, block size 16, WSL2, clocks not locked. A decode step is forward_paged_batch plus argmax and a per-sequence .item(), timed with CUDA events after a sync. Each sequence is prefilled once with the fused rotation; timed steps rewind seq_len. Eager and fused alternate step by step after five warmup steps of each, twenty samples, median. Both sides use the fused RMSNorm. Eager rotation is apply_rope_ref. Fused rotation is one kernel for q and k. Launch counts are a two-step profiler trace of batch 8, context 512. A kernel is charged to the innermost annotation. RoPE is the fusion because the fused-norm profile still had it at 384 launches. The microbench is one rotation of q and k, shape [16, 32, 512, 64], with fp32 cos and sin. Each program reads one contiguous head, so a transposed query is the same stream as this contiguous one. Streaming bytes are one read and one write of q and of k, plus one read of cos and of sin. GB/s uses decimal 1e9 and the median of five windows. The fraction uses the median copy in bench/results/2026-10-31-bandwidth.json.",
